<title>SWITZERLAND: February world air cargo traffic up 4.5pct - ACI.</title>
<headline>February world air cargo traffic up 4.5pct - ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freight and mail traffic handled by 486 airports around the world in February 1997 totalled 3,878,956 million tonnes, according to provisional figures from Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>This was up 4.5 percent on the same month last year, reported Geneva-based ACI</p>
<p>Cargo traffic handled by airports in ACI's six geographical regions in February 1997, with percentage change on February 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>		   February 1997     Pct change from Feb 96</p>
<p>Africa	    16,398 tonnes    up 2.3 percent</p>
<p>Asia/Pacific   789,692 tonnes    up 7.0</p>
<p>Europe	   822,417  tonnes   up 3.4</p>
<p>LatAm/Carib     90,603 tonnes    down 2.4</p>
<p>Middle East    114,078 tonnes    up 2.1</p>
<p>North America 2,045,768 tonnes   up 4.6</p>
<p>Total	   3,878,956 tonnes   up 4.5</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 -   www.racs.com</p>
</text>
